hadiths[38]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24103","Waki narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Salman, he said: Some of the polytheists said while they were mocking him: I see your companion teaches you even defecation. Salman said: Yes, he ordered us not to face the qiblah nor to clean ourselves with our right hands, and not to suffice with fewer than three stones having in them neither dung nor bone."
"24104","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Sharik informed us, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Salman, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to accept the gift and not accept charity."
"24105","Abdullah said, and Ali ibn Hakim narrated it to us, Sharik informed us, from Ubayd al-Mukattib, with his chain, similar to it."
"24106","Abu Said narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Mansur narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, narrated to us, he said: A man said: I see your companion teaches you how you act, such that he even teaches you when one of you goes to the privy. He said: I said: Yes, indeed, even if you mock, he teaches us how one of us goes to the privy, and he forbids us that any of us face the qiblah or turn his back to it, and that any of us clean himself with his right hand, and that any of us wipe with dung or bone, and that he clean himself with fewer than three stones."
"24107","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Zaidah narrated to us, Umar ibn Qays al-Masir narrated to us, from Amr ibn Abi Qurrah, he said: Hudhayfah was at al-Madain, and he used to mention things the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said. Then Hudhayfah came to Salman, and Salman would say: O Hudhayfah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to become angry then speak, and become pleased then speak. I have known that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, addressed and said: Whichever man of my ummah I insulted with an insult in my anger or cursed him with a curse, I am only from the children of Adam, I become angry as they become angry, and I was only sent as a mercy to the worlds, so make it a prayer upon him on the Day of Resurrection."
"24108","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Uthman, he said: I was with Salman al-Farisi under a tree, and he took a dry branch from it and shook it until its leaves fell off. Then he said: O Abu Uthman, will you not ask me why I do this? I said: Why do you do it? He said: This is what the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, did while I was with him under a tree; he took a dry branch from it and shook it until its leaves fell off, then said: O Salman, will you not ask me why I do this? I said: Why do you do it? He said: The Muslim, when he performs ablution and perfects the ablution, then prays the five prayers, his sins fall off as these leaves fall off. And he said: And establish the prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night; indeed good deeds remove evil deeds; that is a reminder for those who remember."
"24109","Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, Sufyan narrated to us, from Mansur and al-Amash, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Salman al-Farisi, he said: The polytheists said to him: We see your companion teaches you such that he teaches you defecation. He said: Yes, he forbids us that any of us clean himself with his right hand or face the qiblah, and forbids us dung and bones, and said: None of you shall clean himself with fewer than three stones."
"24110","Muhammad ibn Jafar narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that a man from the polytheists said to a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him: He taught you this, everything, then he mentioned the hadith."
"24111","Hajjaj ibn Muhammad narrated to us, Ibn Abi Dhib narrated to us, from Said al-Maqburi, he said: My father informed me, from Abdullah ibn Wadi'ah, from Salman al-Khayr, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: No man bathes on Friday and purifies himself as much as he can of purification, and oils from his oil or touches from the perfume of his house, then goes to the mosque and does not separate between two, then prays what Allah has written for him, then listens to the imam when he speaks, except he is forgiven what is between him and the next Friday."
"24112","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mansur, from al-Hasan, he said: When Salman was dying he wept and said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, made a covenant with us, and we abandoned what he covenanted with us, that the provision of one of us from this world be like the provision of a rider. He said: Then we looked at what he left, and the value of what he left was some twenty-odd dirhams or some thirty-odd dirhams."
"24113","Abu Kamil narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Abu Qurrah al-Kindi, from Salman al-Farisi, he said: I was from the sons of the nobles of Persia, then he mentioned the hadith. He said: So I set out, one land raising me and another lowering me, until I passed by a people of Bedouins who enslaved me and sold me until a woman bought me. I heard them mentioning the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and living was hard. I said to her: Grant me a day. She said: Yes. So I set out, gathered firewood, sold it, made food, brought it to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and placed it before him. He said: What is this? I said: Charity. He said to his companions: Eat, and he did not eat. I said: This is one of his signs. Then I stayed as long as Allah willed me to stay. I said to my mistress: Grant me a day. She said: Yes. So I set out, gathered firewood, more than that, made food, brought it to him while he was sitting among his companions, placed it before him. He said: What is this? I said: A gift. He placed his hand and said to his companions: Take, in the name of Allah. I stood behind him, he laid down his cloak, and there was the seal of prophethood. I said: I bear witness that you are the Messenger of Allah. He said: And what is that? I told him about the man, and said: Will he enter Paradise, O Messenger of Allah, for he told me that you are a prophet? He said: None shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul. I said: O Messenger of Allah, he told me that you are a prophet, will he enter Paradise? He said: None shall enter Paradise except a Muslim soul."
"24114","Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Salman, he said: The polytheists said: This one teaches you such that he even teaches you defecation. He said: I said: If you say that, he has forbidden us to face the qiblah or turn our backs to it, or clean ourselves with our right hands, or for one of us to suffice with fewer than three stones, or for one of us to clean himself with dung or bone."
"24115","Yazid narrated to us, Sulayman al-Taymi informed us, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is shy to have the servant stretch his hands to Him asking Him for good and return them empty."
"24116","Yazid narrated to us, a man in the gathering of Amr ibn Ubayd informed us, that he heard Abu Uthman narrating this from Salman al-Farisi, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. Yazid said: Name him for me. They said: He is Jafar ibn Maymun. Abdullah said: My father said, meaning Jafar the seller of carpets."
"24117","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, he said: We were with Salman under a tree, and he took a branch from it and shook it so its leaves fell. He said: Will you not ask me about what I did? We said: Inform us. He said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in the shade of a tree, and he took a branch from it and shook it so its leaves fell. He said: Will you not ask me about what I did? We said: Inform us, O Messenger of Allah. He said: The Muslim servant, when he stands for prayer, his sins fall off him as the leaves of this tree fall off."
"24118","Abd al-Samad narrated to us, Dawud, meaning Ibn Abi al-Furat, narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu Shurayh, from Abu Muslim, freedman of Zayd ibn Suhan al-Abdi, he said: I was with Salman al-Farisi, and he saw a man who had voided and wanted to remove his leather socks, so Salman ordered him to wipe over his leather socks and over his turban and wipe his forelock, and Salman said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over his leather socks and over his head-cover."
"24119","Hushaym narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Qarthaa al-Dabbi, from Salman al-Farisi, he said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Do you know what Friday is? I said: It is the day in which Allah gathered your father therein. He said: But I know what Friday is: No man purifies himself and perfects his purification, then comes to Friday and listens until the imam finishes his prayer, except it will be an expiation for him for what is between it and the coming Friday, as long as killing is avoided."
"24120","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, al-Amash narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: It was said to Salman: Your prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, has taught you everything, even defecation. He said: Yes, he forbade us to face the qiblah with stool or urine, or to clean ourselves with the right hand, or for one of us to clean himself with fewer than three stones, or to clean himself with dung or bone."
"24121","Yahya ibn Said narrated to us, from Sulayman, from Abu Uthman, from Salman, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created one hundred mercies; from them is a mercy by which creatures show mercy to one another; by it wild beasts show affection to their young, and He delayed ninety-nine to the Day of Resurrection."
"24122","Abu Usamah narrated to us, Misar informed me, Umar ibn Qays narrated to me, from Amr ibn Abi Qurrah al-Kindi, he said: My father offered his sister to Salman, and he refused, and married a freedwoman of his called Buqayrah. He said: It reached Abu Qurrah that there was something between Salman and Hudhayfah, so he came seeking him, and was told that he was in a garden of his. He headed to him and met him with a basket containing greens, having put his staff through the handle of the basket while it was on his shoulder. He said: O Abu Abdullah, what was between you and Hudhayfah? Salman says, and man is hasty. They set out until they came to the house of Salman. Salman entered the house and said: Peace be upon you, then gave permission, and there was a rug placed over a door and bricks at his head and earrings. He said: Sit on the bed of your freedwoman which she prepares for herself. He said: Then he began telling him, he said: Hudhayfah used to narrate things the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in his anger to peoples, so I am asked about them, and I say: Hudhayfah knows best what he says, and I dislike that there be hatreds between peoples. Hudhayfah was come to and told: Salman neither confirms you nor denies you in what you say. Hudhayfah came to me and said: O Salman son of Salman's mother. I said: O Hudhayfah son of Hudhayfah's mother, you will stop or I will write to Umar. When I frightened him with Umar he left me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: From the children of Adam am I, so whichever believing servant I cursed with a curse or insulted with an insult undeservedly, make it a prayer upon him."
"24123","Yahya ibn Zakariyya ibn Abi Zaidah narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Ibn Abbas, he said: Salman narrated to me, he said: I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, with food while I was enslaved, and said: This is charity. He ordered his companions and they ate, and he did not eat. Then I came to him with food and said: This is a gift I have gifted to you, honoring you with it, for I saw you do not eat charity. He ordered his companions and they ate, and he ate with them."
"24124","Yahya ibn Zakariyya narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abu Ishaq, from the family of Abu Qurrah, from Salman, he said: I had asked permission of my mistress for that, and she allowed it for me, so I gathered firewood, sold it, and bought that food."
"24125","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri and Affan said, Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu Shurayh, from Abu Muslim, freedman of Zayd ibn Suhan al-Abdi, he said: I was with Salman al-Farisi, and he saw a man who had voided and wanted to remove his leather socks for ablution, so Salman ordered him to wipe over his leather socks and over his turban and wipe his forelock, and Salman said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wipe over his leather socks and over his head-cover."
"24126","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Dhib, from Said al-Maqburi, my father informed me, from Abdullah ibn Wadi'ah, from Salman al-Khayr, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: No man bathes on Friday and purifies himself as much as he can of purification, then oils from his oil or touches from the perfume of his house, then goes and does not separate between two, then prays what was written for him, then listens when the imam speaks, except he is forgiven what is between him and the next Friday."
"24127","al-Zubayri Muhammad ibn Abdullah narrated to us, Israil narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Salman, that he reached a fortress or a city and said to his companions: Let me call them as I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, call them. He said: I was only a man from you, and Allah guided me to Islam; if you accept Islam, for you is what is for us and upon you is what is upon us; if you refuse, pay the jizyah while you are submissive; if you refuse, we declare war upon you equally; Allah does not love the treacherous. He did that with them for three days. When it was the fourth day the people went to it in the morning and conquered it."
"24128","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, Ibn Abi Jafar narrated to us, from Aban ibn Salih, from Ibn Abi Zakariyya al-Khuzai, from Salman al-Khayr, that he heard him while he was narrating to Shurahbil ibn al-Simt while he was stationed on the coast, saying: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Whoever stations a day or a night will have like the fasting of a month for the one sitting, and whoever dies stationed in the path of Allah, Allah will continue for him his reward and what he used to do, the reward of his prayer and fasting and spending, and he is protected from the tribulators of the grave and safe from the greatest terror."
"24129","Muawiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Zaidah, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Jamil ibn Abi Maymunah, from Abu Zakariyya al-Khuzai, from Salman, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Stationing a day and a night in the path of Allah is like the fasting of a month and its standing; if he dies, the reward of the stationed continues upon him until he is resurrected, and he is secured from the tribulators."
"24130","Affan narrated to us, Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Abu Mashar, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Qarthaa al-Dabbi, from Salman al-Farisi, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do you know what Friday is? I said: Yes. He said: I do not know, he claimed, whether he asked him the fourth time or not. He said: I said: It is the day in which his father or your father was gathered. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Shall I not tell you about Friday? No Muslim man purifies himself then walks to the mosque then listens until the imam finishes his prayer, except it will be an expiation for what is between it and the Friday after it, as long as killing is avoided."
"24131","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd informed us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Salman, he said: I contracted with my family to plant for them five hundred young palms, and when they take root I am free. He said: So I came to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and mentioned that to him. He said: Plant and stipulate for them, and when you want to plant, inform me. He said: So I informed him. He said: He came and began planting with his hand except one I planted with my hands, and they took root except the one."
"24132","Shuja ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Qabus ibn Abi Zabyan mentioned it, from his father, from Salman, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: O Salman, do not hate me so you leave your religion. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, how can I hate you, through you Allah guided us? He said: You hate the Arabs so you hate me."
"24133","Affan narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Abu Hashim narrated to us, from Zadhad, from Salman, he said: I read in the Torah: The blessing of food is ablution after it. He said: So I mentioned that to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and told him of what I read in the Torah. He said: The blessing of food is ablution before it and ablution after it."
"24134","Affan narrated to us, Qays ibn al-Rabi narrated to us, Uthman ibn Shabur, a man from Banu Asad, narrated to us, from Shaqiq or similar, Qays doubted, that Salman: A man visited him and he invited him with what he had, and said: Were it not that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, forbade us, or were it not that we were forbidden that one of us burden himself for his companion, I would have burdened myself for you."
"24135","Affan narrated to us, Hammad narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, that Salman besieged a palace of the palaces of Persia and said to his companions: Let me do what I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, do. He praised Allah and extolled Him, then said: I am a man from you, and Allah granted me Islam, and you see the obedience of the Arabs. If you accept Islam and emigrate to us, you are in our position, upon you applies what applies upon us. If you accept Islam and stay in your lands, you are in the position of the Bedouins, for you applies what applies to them and upon you applies what applies upon them. If you refuse and acknowledge the jizyah, for you is what is for the people of jizyah and upon you is what is upon the people of jizyah. He presented that to them for three days, then said to his companions: Attack them, and he conquered it."
"24136","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, Hassan ibn Atiyyah narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Abi Zakariyya, from a man, from Salman, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, he said: Stationing a day and a night is better than the fasting of a month and its standing, fasting not breaking and standing not flagging. If he dies stationed, like his righteous deed continues upon him until he is resurrected, and he is protected from the punishment of the grave."
"24137","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us, Ibn Thawban narrated to us, one who heard Khalid ibn Madan narrating, from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Salman, the like of that."
"24138","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Asim ibn Umar ibn Qatadah al-Ansari narrated to me, from Mahmud ibn Labid, from Abdullah ibn Abbas, he said: Salman al-Farisi narrated to me his hadith from his mouth, he said: I was a Persian man from the people of Isbahan, from a village of it called Jayy, and my father was the dihqan of his village, and I was the most beloved of Allah's creation to him. His love for me did not cease until he confined me in his house, meaning attendant of the fire, as the slave-girl is confined. I strove in Magianism until I was the keeper of the fire who kindles it, not letting it die for an hour. He said: My father had a great estate. He said: He was busy with a building of his one day and said to me: O my son, I have been busy with a building this day from my estate, so go and look after it, and he ordered me in it some of what he wanted. I set out intending his estate and passed by a church of the Christians, heard their voices in it while they were praying, and I did not know the affair of people due to my father confining me in his house. When I passed by them and heard their voices I entered upon them to see what they do. He said: When I saw them their prayer pleased me and I desired their affair, and said: This, by Allah, is better than the religion we are upon. By Allah, I did not leave them until the sun set, and I left my father's estate and did not go to it. I said to them: Where is the origin of this religion? They said: In al-Sham. He said: Then I returned to my father, and he had sent in search of me and I had distracted him from all his work. He said: When I came to him he said: O my son, where were you? Did I not entrust to you what I entrusted? He said: I said: O my father, I passed by people praying in a church of theirs, and what I saw of their religion pleased me. By Allah, I remained with them until the sun set. He said: O my son, there is no good in that religion; your religion and the religion of your fathers is better than it. He said: I said: No, by Allah, it is better than our religion. He said: He feared me and put a shackle on my legs, then confined me in his house. He said: The Christians sent to me, and I said to them: When a party comes to you from al-Sham, Christian merchants, inform me of them. He said: A party from al-Sham, Christian merchants, came to them. He said: They informed me of them. He said: I said to them: When they finish their needs and want to return to their lands, notify me of them. He said: When they wanted to return to their lands they informed me of them, so I cast off the iron from my legs, then left with them until I reached al-Sham. When I reached it I said: Who is the best of the people of this religion? They said: The bishop in the church. He said: I came to him and said: I have desired this religion and loved to be with you, serve you in your church, learn from you, and pray with you. He said: Enter, so I entered with him. He said: He was an evil man, ordering them with charity and urging them in it, and when they gathered to him things from it he hoarded it for himself and did not give the poor, until he gathered seven jars of gold and silver. He said: I hated him with severe hatred for what I saw him do. Then he died, and the Christians gathered to him to bury him. I said to them: This was an evil man, ordering you with charity and urging you in it, and when you brought it to him he hoarded it for himself and did not give the poor anything from it. They said: What is your knowledge of that? He said: I said: I will show you his treasure. They said: Show us it. He said: I showed them its place. He said: They extracted from it seven jars filled with gold and silver. He said: When they saw them they said: By Allah, we will never bury him. They crucified him, then stoned him with stones. Then they brought another man and put him in his place. He said: Salman says: I never saw a man who does not pray the five, I think, better than him, more ascetic in this world, more desirous of the Hereafter, nor more diligent night and day than him. He said: I loved him with a love I had not loved before him, and stayed with him a time. Then death came to him and I said to him: O so-and-so, I was with you and loved you with a love I had not loved before you, and what you see of the decree of Allah has come to you, so to whom do you commend me and what do you order me? He said: O my son, by Allah, I do not know anyone today upon what I was upon; people have perished and changed and left most of what they were upon, except a man at al-Mawsil, and he is so-and-so, and he is upon what I was upon, so join him. He said: When he died and was buried I joined the companion of al-Mawsil and said to him: O so-and-so, so-and-so commended me at his death to join you, and told me that you are upon his affair. He said: He said to me: Stay with me, so I stayed with him and found him the best man upon the affair of his companion. He did not remain but to die, and when death came to him I said to him: O so-and-so, so-and-so commended me to you and ordered me to join you, and what you see of the decree of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has come to you, so to whom do you commend me and what do you order me? He said: O my son, by Allah, I do not know a man upon the like of what we were upon except at Nasibin, and he is so-and-so, so join him. He said: When he died and was buried I joined the companion of Nasibin, came to him, told him my story and what my companion ordered me. He said: Stay with me, so I stayed with him and found him upon the affair of his two companions. I stayed with the best man. By Allah, he did not remain but death befell him, and when he came I said to him: O so-and-so, so-and-so had commended me to so-and-so, then so-and-so commended me to you, so to whom do you commend me and what do you order me? He said: O my son, by Allah, we do not know anyone remaining upon our affair I order you to come to him except a man at Ammuriyyah, for he is upon the like of what we are upon; if you like, go to him. He said: He is upon our affair. He said: When he died and was buried I joined the companion of Ammuriyyah and told him my story. He said: Stay with me, so I stayed with a man upon the guidance of his companions and their affair. He said: I earned until I had cows and small sheep. He said: Then the decree of Allah befell him, and when he came I said to him: O so-and-so, I was with so-and-so, and so-and-so commended me to so-and-so, and so-and-so commended me to so-and-so, then so-and-so commended me to you, so to whom do you commend me and what do you order me? He said: O my son, by Allah, I do not know anyone who has come to be upon what we were upon from people I order you to come to him, but the time of a prophet has shaded you, he is sent with the religion of Ibrahim, emerging in the land of the Arabs, emigrating to a land between two lava tracts, between them palms, with marks not hidden: he eats the gift and does not eat charity, between his shoulders is the seal of prophethood. If you can join that land, do. He said: Then he died and was buried. I stayed at Ammuriyyah as long as Allah willed me to stay. Then a group from Kalb, merchants, passed by me and I said to them: Carry me to the land of the Arabs and I will give you these cows of mine and these sheep of mine. They said: Yes. I gave them them and they carried me, until when they brought me to Wadi al-Qura they wronged me and sold me to a man from the Jews as a slave. I was with him and saw the palms, and hoped it be the town my companion described to me, and it did not settle in myself. While I was with him, a cousin of his from Madinah, from Banu Qurayzah, came to him, bought me from him, carried me to Madinah. By Allah, it was only that I saw it and recognized it by the description of my companion. I stayed in it, and Allah sent His messenger, and he stayed in Makkah as he stayed, I hearing no mention of him with what I was in of the busyness of slavery. Then he emigrated to Madinah. By Allah, I was at the top of a date-cluster of my master working in it some work, my master sitting, when a cousin of his came until he stood upon him and said: So-and-so, may Allah fight Banu Qaylah, by Allah they are now gathered at Quba upon a man who came to them from Makkah today claiming he is a prophet. He said: When I heard it trembling seized me until I thought I would fall upon my master. He said: I came down from the palm and began saying to his cousin: What, what do you say, what do you say? He said: My master became angry and struck me a severe blow, then said: What is yours and this? Attend to your work. He said: I said: Nothing, I only wanted to verify what he said. I had something I had gathered, and when evening came I took it, then went to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at Quba, entered upon him, said to him: It has reached me that you are a righteous man and with you are companions of yours, strangers with need, and this is something I had for charity, and I saw you more deserving of it than others. He said: I brought it near to him, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: Eat, and withheld his hand and did not eat. He said: I said in myself: This is one. Then I left him, gathered something, and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, moved to Madinah. Then I came with it and said: I saw you do not eat charity, and this is a gift I have honored you with. He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ate from it and ordered his companions and they ate with him. He said: I said in myself: These are two. Then I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while he was at Baqi al-Gharqad. He said: He had followed a funeral of his companions, upon him two garments of his, while he was sitting among his companions. I greeted him, then turned to look at his back whether I see the seal my companion described to me. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saw me turning around, he knew I was verifying something described to me. He said: He cast his cloak from his back, I looked at the seal and recognized it. I fell upon him kissing him and weeping. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Move, so I moved. I told him my story as I told you, O Ibn Abbas. He said: It pleased the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that his companions hear that. Then slavery busied Salman until Badr and Uhud with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed him by. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Contract, O Salman. I contracted with my master for three hundred palms I revive for him with the young shoots, and forty ounces. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to his companions: Help your brother. They helped me with palms, a man with thirty saplings, a man with twenty, a man with fifteen, a man with ten, meaning a man according to what he had, until three hundred saplings gathered for me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to me: Go, O Salman, and dig for them, and when you finish come to me, I will place them with my hands. I dug for them and my companions helped me, until when I finished them I came to him and told him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went out with me to them, and we began bringing near to him the saplings and the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, placing them with his hand. By the One in whose hand is Salman's soul, not one sapling of them died. I paid the palms and money remained upon me. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought the like of a chicken egg of gold from some of the raids and said: What has the Persian contracted one done? He said: I was called for him and said: Take this and pay with it what is upon you, O Salman. I said: Where will this fall, O Messenger of Allah, from what is upon me? He said: Take it, for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will pay with it from you. He said: I took it and weighed to them from it, by the One in whose hand is Salman's soul, forty ounces, paid them their right, was freed, witnessed with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, al-Khandaq, then no battle with him passed me by."
"24139","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, from a man from Banu Abd al-Qays, from Salman al-Khayr, he said: When I said: Where will this fall from what is upon me, O Messenger of Allah, the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took it and turned it on his tongue, then said: Take it and pay them from it. I took it and paid them from it all their right, forty ounces."
"24140","Ali ibn Asim narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Saib, from Abu al-Bakhtari, he said: Salman al-Farisi besieged a palace of the palaces of Persia, and his companions said to him: O Abu Abdullah, will you not attack them? He said: No, until I call them as the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to call them. He said: He came to them and spoke to them, he said: I am a Persian man, I am from you, and the Arabs obey me. Choose one of three: either you accept Islam, or you give the jizyah from hand while you are submissive, unpraised, or we declare war upon you and fight you. They said: We will not accept Islam nor give the jizyah, but we will declare war upon you. Salman returned to his companions. They said: Will you not attack them? He said: No. He said: He called them for three days and they did not accept, so he fought them and conquered it."
